/*
  Localizable.strings — German.

  Keys are the English text, exactly as in en.lproj. A key that does not match
  character for character silently falls back to English, and nothing in the
  build says so, which is why tools/check-translations.py compares the two key
  sets rather than trusting that they match.

  The wording is shared with android/app/src/main/res/values-de/strings.xml,
  for the reason the English copy is shared: one product must not name a status
  "Am Schauen" on one phone and something else on the other.

  Two decisions, both explained in docs/LOCALISATION.md:

  "Benachrichtigungen", not Apple's house term "Mitteilungen". The platforms
  disagree about this word and this project's copy does not vary by platform;
  the Android word is understood on both.

  "du", not "Sie". The English copy is plain and direct, and "Sie" would turn
  the same sentences into a bank's.
*/

